<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13051"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 11:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->2004-Nov. 5--Sgt. Henry Spurlock, Officer Keith Goodall and Deputy Michael Wint were in the area looking for a suspect who ran from a traffic stop and responded to the report of noises near the back of a residence at 6220 N. Independence. David T. Bennett of Wichita reportedly was found hiding in a shed attached to the back of the residence and had taken the homeowner’s red nylon jacket and brown baseball cap to disguise himself, the officers reported. <BR> <BR>Nov. 5--Officer Keith Goodall and Sgt. Henry Spurlock searched David T. Bennett’s vehicle and reported finding a Coast to Coast 12-gauge black shotgun loaded with three lugs, and a black Orion semi-automatic pistol loaded with 9mm hollow points in a black leather jacket at 1000 E. 61st North. <BR> <BR>Nov. 5--Officer Keith Goodall reported assisting Deputy Black with a strip search of David T. Bennett in the jail and finding marijuana under the sole of his Nike tennis shoes. Bennett was charged with trafficking contraband in a penal institution. <BR> <BR>Nov. 5--Officer Keith Goodall reported booking David T. Bennett of Wichita on a Sedgwick County Sheriff’s Department warrant at 141 W. Elm. The parole violation warrant was for aggravated robbery with a $75,000 bond. <BR> <BR>Nov. 5--Officer Keith Goodall reported booking David T. Bennett of Wichita for a misdemeanor warrant through the Geary County Sheriff’s Department at 141 W. Elm. <BR> <BR>Nov. 5--Officer Keith Goodall reported booking David T. Bennett of Wichita for a misdemeanor warrant through the Rose Hill Police Department at 141 W. Elm. <BR> <BR>  <BR>Nov. 4--Officers reported four juveniles smoking marijuana in front of a residence in the 6200 block of Independence. One was arrested and taken to the Juvenile Intake Assessment Center. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>WHAT is this all about? <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13051-->
<!--Post: 13052--><!--Time: 1114024178-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13052"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 12:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If David T. Bennet is still in jail it would be nice to talk to him. <BR>HMMMMMMMMMMMMMM <BR>Guess Denny didn&#39;t like no pot smokin teens &#39;round his and the mrs. house <BR>or on his and mrs. street <BR>What IS this all about <BR>Rocky - would your father or any other neighbors know?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13052-->
<!--Post: 13060--><!--Time: 1114046678-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13060"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 6:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Else - My Mom and I used to sit at the kitchen table and laugh about some of these police reports in the Ark Valley paper. It seemed if the neighbor across the street &#34;farted&#34; it was printed in the next issue of the ark valley paper. LOL! Really, it is a great lil paper. Nevertheless, my Mom before she got sick knew everything about everbody and yes it seemed in the last few years the hood was really going down hill with drugs. &#40;I mentioned that under another post &#34;changing penal system&#34;&#41; <BR> <BR>My Dad has mentioned on several occassions recently that he remembers when the police were at Rader&#39;s house last year, and I thought that the PCPD had really screwed up not arresting him then. Then my Dad showed me the Ark Valley paper with the same report posted above, and I realized that again they had no probable cause to suspect Rader of anything. This idiot just ended up in his back yard. <BR> <BR>As for the juveniles smoking pot, we&#39;ll that doesn&#39;t surprise me either. I&#39;ve mentioned that there is a park behind Rader&#39;s house - well we were all home this last Christmas and my daughters and nephews went over to the park to play basketball. They encountered a foul mouthed lil 6 year old kid that they are convinced was the devil. Then they watched this same kid&#39;s mother walk over to the basketball court and light a joint up, while the lil kid was cursing her the whole time. My kids and nephews came home and were astonished that such language could come out of such a lil kid. Later that same evening my oldest daughter had walked across the street to the QTrip, and was minding her own business when these two punks approached her &#40;with me standing there&#41;and called her a &#42;#@#^&amp;&#40; beotch. They didn&#39;t know her from Adam. I thought we were going to jail for assault for sure. Because my oldest doesn&#39;t take crap off of anyone, ever! Especially, men! We&#39;ll these weren&#39;t men. Anyway, at that same Qtrip I got flashed some gang signs for backing out of a parking spot. My sister and I laughed about that because I certainly didn&#39;t look like someone that would understand what this punk flashed me anyway. So why bother, I guess it made him feel better.  <BR> <BR>Anyway, had any of us kids in that neighborhood, when we were growing up, stepped out of line the entire neighborhood knew about it. And all the neighbors were like police watch dogs watching over all the kids. If you did anything inappropriate and a neighbor saw it, or heard it,  you were going to be in trouble. Tom Hedge &#40;Marine&#39;s husband&#41;he saw me once throwing rocks at a boy that called me a name, so he made me put the rocks down and then he called that boys mom and told her what he called me. HA! He didn&#39;t like it when the boys picked on the lil girls, but trust me we could hold our own too!  <BR> <BR>You know, now that I think about this - my Mom was always more concerend about another neighbor involved in criminal activity. That&#39;s funny, because it wasn&#39;t Rader. I think Mom figured she had DTDC under wraps and may be even feared her after she bitched him out for not picking up that tree limb out of the street. HA! LOL! Hey - may be that was printed in the Ark Valley paper.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13060-->
<!--Post: 13075--><!--Time: 1114081850-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13075"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 21, 2005 - 4:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, what about the lady at 6225? I found dozen if not more of her calling the cops because she was ill. Is this the same lady that sent her daughter across the street to call 911 at raders house? Is she really ill, or whats the deal? <BR> <BR>About the first post in this thread, can dtdc <BR>say he doesnt know about the stuff in his shed, this punk bennett must have put it there. <BR>He was found in the shed. Could that have tainted anything?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13075-->
<!--Post: 13110--><!--Time: 1114192422-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13110"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 10:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty - I&#39;m still working on that one with a confirmation from my Dad. &#40;I wish Mom was still here she could tell you anything you ever wanted to know about people in the hood including DTDC&#41;. I&#39;m fairly certain that she is the one that is sick and did send her daughter across the street to make a 911 call. I&#39;ll wait untill I here from Dad. <BR> <BR>Itty - Dare I say, the evidence being tainted in that shed from the idiot falling into it could be a good argument for the Defense team.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13110-->
<!--Post: 13123--><!--Time: 1114218668-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13123"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 6:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok, I don&#39;t if this is the same woman, but she apparently has asthma and repeatedly will call the paramedics to get oxygen. Dad said, she always refuses to go to the hospital and the ambulance is there at least 3 times a month.  <BR> <BR>The idiot - Dad mentioned by name&#40;it is not Bennett&#41; and his family lives in the neighborhood. Dad said that this kid has been heavily involved with drugs for some time and that evening he was running from the police and sought hiding in Rader&#39;s shed. The large shed in the back yard, not the one attached to the back of his house. The small shed attached to the back of Rader&#39;s house is the one that all the evidence was found in, according to CNN.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13123-->
<!--Post: 13125--><!--Time: 1114219721-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13125"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 22, 2005 - 6:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Rocky!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13125-->
<!--Post: 13161--><!--Time: 1114441364-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13161"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 25, 2005 - 8:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank Rocky... and thanks to your Father Too!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13161-->
<!--Post: 13283--><!--Time: 1114778958-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13283"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 5:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->more 6220 stories: <BR> <BR>2005-March 13--Officer Dwight Wilkes reported the mailbox had been pushed over into the street without being damaged at 6220 N. Independence. It was stored on the back side of the house, the officer reported. <BR> <BR>2005-March 11--Lt. Eric Miller responded to the report of people possibly taking items at 6220 N. Independence. <BR> <BR> <BR>2005-March 6--Officers Terrell Brown and Hobert Capps responded to the report of news media allegedly harassing an identified woman at 6314 N. Jacksonville. The media was across the street, taking photos of a residence, the officers reported. She was advised that as long as they were not on her property, they could take photos. No criminal activity was discovered. <BR> <BR>2005-March 5--Officers Terry Love and Dwight Wilkes and Police Chief William Ball stood by for several hours as family members retrieved items from the home at 6200 N. Independence. They also wrote tickets for those who disregarded a traffic control device. <BR> <BR>March 5--Officers Terry Love and Dwight Wilkes conducted traffic enforcement in the 6200 block of North Independence. <BR> <BR>March 5--Officer Terrell Brown responded to the report of a yelling match between an identified person and three people driving by in a maroon Jeep Liberty in the 6200 block of Independence. <BR> <BR>2005-March 4--Officer Terry Love responded to the report of an elderly man and woman being in the yard and taking photos at 6220 Independence. He counseled them about trespassing and encouraged them to leave the area. They did so, the officer reported. He replaced traffic barricades on 61st North. <BR> <BR>March 2--Detective Timothy Dye and Officer Dwight Wilkes reported observing two juvenile males taking items without permission from 6220 N. Independence. Both were released after they returned the stolen items, and their parents were called and advised of what their children were doing, the officers reported. <BR> <BR>March 1--Officers conducted traffic enforcemnt in the area of 6200 N. Independence in an effort to keep traffic moving and people off of residents’ lawns. <BR>March 1--Samuel Winegarner of 6235 N. Independence was ticketed for blocking traffic in the 6200 block of Independence by parking his jeep and motorcycle across both lanes of traffic to keep people from driving up and down the street, officers reported. <BR> <BR>March 1--Officers reported placing street signs and pylons on Independence, and did several checks on a residence at 6220 N. Independence. <BR> <BR>Feb. 28--Officers Terrell Brown and Kevin Werlein assisted members of the Rader family as they collected belongings at 6314 N. Jacksonville, then escorted them from the residence to the bank and just south of the Park City limits, at the request of Police Chief William Ball. <BR> <BR>2005-April 16--Sgt. Trent Johnson responded to the report of people moving items out of 6220 N. Independence and that the media was on the scene. <BR> <BR>2005-March26--Officer Hobert Capps responded to the report of a trespasser at the Rader residence, 6220 N. Independence. An identified man and woman were contacted in their vehicle parked on the street in front of the residence. The man apologized and said he did not damage or take any property, the officer reported. <BR> <BR>2005-March 11--Lt. Eric Miller responded to the report of people possibly taking items at 6220 N. Independence <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13283-->
<!--Post: 13296--><!--Time: 1114821735-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13296"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 5:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty, when Weingarner parked his jeep and motorcycle in the middle of the street to stop the lookyloos I knew then that the situation was just going to fester. So, I emailed the mayor the next morning and mentioned the public safety issues and the barricades went back up. They have since been taken down, but at the time it was crazy. Dad told me people still drive by, but nothing like then.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13296-->
<!--Post: 13297--><!--Time: 1114821970-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13297"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 5:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, it sound crazy. Hopefully, it will settle down soon. It is nice to have you here to give us the scoop.  later, itty <BR> <BR>ps-Im taking the whole weekend off from my puter, so you guys post some good stuff for me to read monday morning!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
